Solutions to all seventeen lettered parts. Use <natural units>, the <Minkowski metric> $g_{\mu\nu}=\operatorname{diag}(1,-1,-1,-1)$, <Feynman slash notation> $\not p=\gamma^\mu p_\mu$, and the <Feynman i-epsilon prescription> in internal <propagators>. Define the <scattering amplitude> by $S_{fi}=\delta_{fi}+i(2\pi)^4\delta^{(4)}(p_f-p_i)\mathcal M_{fi}$. The <gauge covariant derivative> convention in question 3 is specified there to match the printed three-boson <Feynman rule>.

